{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"One program, four surfaces — Python, the CLI, Rust and TypeScript\"\n",
        "---"
      ],
      "id": "41651e52"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# | echo: false\n",
        "import jammi_cookbook"
      ],
      "id": "bf8101c2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Recipe:** `jammi sources add` · `jammi embed` · `jammi search` (the CLI) ·\n",
        "`InferenceSession::add_source` / `generate_text_embeddings` / `search_by_id` (Rust) ·\n",
        "`catalog.addSource` / `embedding.generateEmbeddings` / `embedding.search` (TypeScript,\n",
        "`@f-inverse/jammi-client`) · `add_source` / `generate_embeddings` / `search` (Python) ·\n",
        "**Rail:** parity (one program, the same rows on every surface).\n",
        "\n",
        "Every other chapter reaches the engine from Python. Python is one of four surfaces: the\n",
        "`jammi` command line, the Rust crates, and the TypeScript client drive the same engine\n",
        "through the same verbs. This chapter writes one small program — register a source, embed\n",
        "it, search it — and runs it on all four, then checks that they return the same rows.\n",
        "\n",
        "The CLI, the TypeScript client and Python's remote arm talk to one server over the\n",
        "`jammi.v1` wire; the Rust program links the engine in process, the way the Rust\n",
        "quickstart does. So the chapter checks two properties at once: every surface exposes\n",
        "the program, and the in-process engine and the server agree.\n",
        "\n",
        "## The program and the server\n",
        "\n",
        "The corpus is the twenty-row `tiny_corpus` and the encoder the tiny BERT checkpoint the\n",
        "book ships, so every surface finishes in seconds once built. The query is by example:\n",
        "the rows nearest the vector stored for row `1`. Every surface can ask it without a text\n",
        "encoder of its own.\n"
      ],
      "id": "bb831752"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import contextlib\n",
        "import importlib.metadata\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import subprocess\n",
        "import tempfile\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "import jammi\n",
        "from jammi.testing import LiveServer\n",
        "from jammi_cookbook import contracts, fixtures, programs\n",
        "\n",
        "VERSION = importlib.metadata.version(\"jammi-ai\")\n",
        "CORPUS = fixtures.url(\"tiny_corpus.parquet\")\n",
        "MODEL = fixtures.model(\"tiny_bert\")\n",
        "ROW_KEY = \"1\"\n",
        "work = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"jammi_surfaces_\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "stack = contextlib.ExitStack()\n",
        "server = stack.enter_context(LiveServer(work / \"server\"))\n",
        "print(f\"jammi {VERSION}; server at {server.endpoint}\")\n",
        "print(f\"built from {'this checkout' if programs.checkout() else 'the release'}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def rows(records) -> list[tuple[int, float]]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Ranked `(id, similarity)` pairs, similarity to five places.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return [(int(r[\"id\"]), round(float(r[\"similarity\"]), 5)) for r in records]"
      ],
      "id": "d5f8197a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Python\n"
      ],
      "id": "8a12683d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "with jammi.connect(server.endpoint) as db:\n",
        "    db.add_source(\"corpus_py\", url=CORPUS, format=\"parquet\")\n",
        "    db.generate_embeddings(source=\"corpus_py\", model=MODEL, columns=[\"content\"], key=\"id\")\n",
        "    hits = db.search(\"corpus_py\", row_key=ROW_KEY, k=3, select=[\"id\", \"similarity\"])\n",
        "python_rows = rows(hits.to_pylist())\n",
        "print(python_rows)"
      ],
      "id": "7c5bd91f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The command line\n",
        "\n",
        "The `jammi` binary is a strict client of a running server. `jammi embed` and\n",
        "`jammi search` are its data verbs, beside the control verbs (`sources`, `models`,\n",
        "`jobs` and the rest). `search` prints its rows as JSON lines, one object per row in rank\n",
        "order, so a shell pipeline or a script reads them exactly.\n"
      ],
      "id": "02c89385"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "jammi_cli = programs.cli(VERSION)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def cli(*args: str) -> str:\n",
        "    return subprocess.run([jammi_cli, \"--target\", server.endpoint, *args],\n",
        "                          capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "print(cli(\"sources\", \"add\", \"corpus_cli\", \"--url\", CORPUS, \"--format\", \"parquet\"))\n",
        "print(cli(\"embed\", \"corpus_cli\", \"--model\", MODEL, \"--columns\", \"content\", \"--key\", \"id\"))\n",
        "cli_out = cli(\"search\", \"corpus_cli\", \"--row-key\", ROW_KEY, \"-k\", \"3\",\n",
        "              \"--select\", \"id,similarity\")\n",
        "print(cli_out)\n",
        "cli_rows = rows(json.loads(line) for line in cli_out.splitlines())"
      ],
      "id": "2889c5ef",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Rust\n",
        "\n",
        "The Rust program is the Rust quickstart's shape: an `InferenceSession` over a\n",
        "`JammiConfig`, the engine linked into the binary, with no server. Its artifact directory comes\n",
        "from the environment, as any other setting would.\n"
      ],
      "id": "6b2b06d3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print((programs.program(\"one_program\") / \"main.rs\").read_text())"
      ],
      "id": "ef73dfe0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "It builds against the crates of this release: from crates.io in a fresh runtime, or from\n",
        "the workspace when the book renders in a checkout. The first build compiles the engine,\n",
        "so it takes minutes; a rerun takes seconds.\n"
      ],
      "id": "70f03d37"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "project = programs.rust_program(work, VERSION, \"one_program\")\n",
        "rust_env = dict(os.environ, JAMMI_ARTIFACT_DIR=str(work / \"rust\"))\n",
        "build = subprocess.run([programs.cargo(), \"run\", \"-q\", \"--manifest-path\",\n",
        "                        str(project / \"Cargo.toml\"), \"--\", CORPUS, MODEL, ROW_KEY],\n",
        "                       capture_output=True, text=True, env=rust_env)\n",
        "assert build.returncode == 0, build.stderr[-4000:]\n",
        "print(build.stdout)\n",
        "rust_rows = rows(json.loads(line) for line in build.stdout.splitlines())"
      ],
      "id": "fdb845e1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## TypeScript\n",
        "\n",
        "The TypeScript client speaks gRPC-web over `fetch`, so the same script runs in Node, a\n",
        "browser, or a Worker. It reads the search result, an Arrow IPC stream, with Apache\n",
        "Arrow's JavaScript library.\n"
      ],
      "id": "e1bfb054"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print((programs.program(\"one_program\") / \"search.ts\").read_text())"
      ],
      "id": "33302795",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ts_project, ts_env = programs.ts_program(work, VERSION)\n",
        "http = server.endpoint.replace(\"grpc://\", \"http://\")\n",
        "ts = subprocess.run([str(ts_project / \"node_modules\" / \".bin\" / \"tsx\"), \"search.ts\",\n",
        "                     http, CORPUS, MODEL, ROW_KEY],\n",
        "                    cwd=ts_project, capture_output=True, text=True, env=ts_env)\n",
        "assert ts.returncode == 0, ts.stderr[-4000:]\n",
        "print(ts.stdout)\n",
        "ts_rows = rows(json.loads(line) for line in ts.stdout.splitlines())\n",
        "stack.close()"
      ],
      "id": "ca073fbf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The same rows\n"
      ],
      "id": "0a7b2ba0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "surfaces = {\"Python\": python_rows, \"CLI\": cli_rows, \"Rust\": rust_rows,\n",
        "            \"TypeScript\": ts_rows}\n",
        "print(f\"{'surface':<12}{'ranked (id, similarity)'}\")\n",
        "for name, ranked in surfaces.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"{name:<12}{ranked}\")\n",
        "agreeing = sum(ranked == python_rows for ranked in surfaces.values())\n",
        "print(f\"surfaces agreeing with Python: {agreeing} of {len(surfaces)}\")"
      ],
      "id": "8c9febd4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# | echo: false\n",
        "assert agreeing == len(surfaces), surfaces\n",
        "contracts.assert_close(\"surfaces.agreeing\", agreeing, tol=0.0)\n",
        "contracts.assert_close(\"surfaces.nearest_id\", python_rows[1][0], tol=0.0)\n",
        "contracts.assert_close(\"surfaces.nearest_similarity\", python_rows[1][1], tol=1e-4)"
      ],
      "id": "8680b380",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "All four surfaces return the same three rows in the same order, with the same\n",
        "similarities: row `1` itself, then its two nearest neighbours. The program is the same\n",
        "three verbs in each language — register, embed, search — because every surface is a\n",
        "binding of the one `jammi.v1` vocabulary, and the in-process engine behind the Rust\n",
        "program is the same engine behind the server."
      ],
      "id": "2d3032b1"
    }
  ],
